'" Generated from file 'request.man' by tcllib/doctools with format 'nroff'
.TH "request" n 1.0 tcllib "HTTP request wrapper module"
.SH NAME
request \- TclOO wrapper for HTTP requests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B package require request
.B request create client
.B client configure -method GET -url https://www.example.com
.B set body [client execute]
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
The request package provides a TclOO class named request that wraps the
standard Tcl [cmd ::http::geturl] and [cmd ::http::posturl] interfaces.
It stores request parameters on the object, executes the request with
[cmd execute], and validates that the HTTP response code is in the 2xx range.

.SH ATTRIBUTES
.TP
.B method
The HTTP method to use for the request, such as GET, POST, PUT, or DELETE.

.TP
.B url
The request URI.

.TP
.B body
The request body payload for POST or other methods that accept a body.

.TP
.B headers
A list of HTTP headers to pass to the underlying http command.

.TP
.B opts
Additional options forwarded directly to the http package.

.SH METHODS
.TP
.B configure ?options?
Set stored request attributes or return the current configuration as a dictionary
when called without arguments.

.TP
.B cget attr
Return the named request or response attribute value. Valid keys include
method, url, body, headers, opts, lastBody, lastCode, lastStatus, lastMeta,
and lastToken.

.TP
.B execute
Execute the stored request and return the response body on success. Throws
an error if the request fails or the HTTP status is not in the 2xx range.

.TP
.B request method url ?body? ?headers? ?opts?
Perform a one-shot request and return a list with body, code, status, headers,
and token.

.TP
.B get url ?headers? ?opts?
Convenience wrapper for a GET request.

.TP
.B post url ?body? ?headers? ?opts?
Convenience wrapper for a POST request.

.TP
.B lastResponse
Return the last response properties as a list.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.B package require request
request create client
client configure -method GET -url https://www.example.com
set body [client execute]
puts $body
.fi

.nf
.B package require request
request create client -method POST -url https://api.example.com/submit \
    -body {name=alice&action=save} -headers {Content-Type application/x-www-form-urlencoded}
set body [client execute]
puts $body
.fi

.nf
.B package require request
request create client
client configure {
    method POST
    url https://api.example.com/submit
    headers {Content-Type application/json}
    body {"name":"alice"}
}
try {
    set body [client execute]
    puts $body
} on error {type msg} {
    puts stderr "Request failed ($type): $msg"
}
.fi
